    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "# DUNCAN PRIME MASTER — SINGLE PRODUCT STREAM R02\n\nSTATUS = ACTIVE SINGLE PRODUCT / MASTER STREAM\nROOT = DUNCAN PRIME\nDURABLE RESET = comment `5506451195`\nMAIN_AT_RESET = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nBRANCH = `duncan/zorr-studio-r01`\n\n## PURPOSE\nReplace the previous parallel CHAT A / B / C execution topology with one authoritative product stream after repeated stale-state / competing-NEXT regressions.\n\n## ACTIVE TOPOLOGY\n`ONE ACTIVE PRODUCT STREAM = #251`\n\n- #249 parallel CHAT A topology = retired / historical workstream.\n- #250 parallel CHAT B topology = retired after PREP delivery; its camera/S001 contracts remain reusable evidence.\n- #248 = supporting costume-mechanics QC library, not the active universal hard gate.\n- SHERIFF = independent evidence/discipline monitor only, never a product executor.\n- Automations may monitor or perform one explicitly delegated bounded task but may not create a competing `ACTIVE_BASE`, product route, or NEXT.\n\n## CURRENT PROVEN FOUNDATION\n- #245 `FULL_CHARACTER_MODEL_LOCK_R02 = PASS` remains the locked character-model foundation.\n- Existing accepted character pack / C00 references remain authority; do not reopen generic BODY/HAIR/HANDS or source recovery without fresh contradictory evidence.\n- #250 PREP artifacts for camera/S001 are reusable and do not need to be recreated.\n\n## #248 ROLE AFTER RESET\nThe six costume controls remain useful diagnostics/QC rules.\n\n`W01 ARM_RAISE` is a high-information shoulder/armhole/lapel/armpit mechanics control, but it is **not a mandatory film frame** and is no longer a standalone prerequisite for every unrelated production pose.\n\nApply the relevant #248 control(s) to actual production key drawings when that force exists. Run standalone diagnostics only when a real product artifact exposes a concrete mechanics uncertainty/regression.\n\n## ACTIVE PRODUCT OBJECTIVE\n`FIRST_REAL_PRODUCTION_KEY_DRAWING / SCENE-BOUND POSE CANDIDATE`\n\nProduct-first sequence:\n`REAL PRODUCT ARTIFACT -> RELEVANT IDENTITY/BODY/COSTUME/POSE QC -> REPAIR ONLY FAILED LAYER -> CAMERA/S001 BINDING WHEN LEGAL -> NEXT REAL ARTIFACT`\n\nDo not create synthetic gate artifacts merely to prove process when the same invariant can be checked on the real product drawing.\n\n## HARD LAWS\n- GitHub fresh evidence wins.\n- One active base / one active product NEXT.\n- No new parallel chat topology.\n- No source/Krita/OpenToonz rediscovery unless a fresh real product blocker requires it.\n- No PASS from schedule/activity/summary.\n- No character/costume redesign by accident.\n- No W01-specific fixation unless the actual production pose uses that force or a concrete regression calls for the diagnostic.\n\n## OUTPUT CONTRACT\n`RESULT / DELTA / EVIDENCE / NEXT`\n\nEvery NEXT must point to one real product artifact or one exact first broken layer that blocks that artifact.",
